  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 126 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will arrive over Iowa on Tuesday as a large \ntrough develops over the Western CONUS. The ridge will transition \nto southwest flow Tuesday night into Wednesday. A short wave will \nlift through the southwest flow and will bring low precipitation \nchances to the state. Precipitation chances will hinge on return \nmoisture and the potential for any saturation given the antecedent \nvery dry mass. The surface high will have moved east enough for a \nGulf moisture link to occur but this moisture may not be enough for \nwidespread precipitation. A more significant upper low will enter \nthe southwest CONUS late in the week and will begin to translate \neastward towards next weekend. That system appears to present a \ngreater chance for more widespread precipitation. Temperatures will \nwarm from the 50s to the 50s and 60s by Wednesday through\nFriday. The wind will be breezy to gusty at times at times. Wind\ngusts of 30 to 40 mph look possible Wednesday.",
